    {
      "reviewId": "Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tWaE9FeGZRVVZzUTAxRE5uWlNOakIwYWtOelFWRRAB",
      "authorName": "cutelady baluch",
      "starRating": 5,
      "reviewDate": "2 weeks ago",
      "localGuideInfo": "Local Guide · 2.7K reviews",
      "text": "The People’s Great Hall of Chongqing is an iconic landmark that blends traditional Chinese architectural elements with grand scale. Built in the 1950s, it resembles the Temple of Heaven in Beijing and serves as a symbol of the city’s resilience and pride. Surrounded by People’s Square, it offers a striking view both day and night, especially when lit up. Whether you’re a history buff, architecture lover, or just exploring downtown Chongqing, this is a must-see cultural highlight.",
      "scrapedAt": "2026-03-23T07:08:35.974Z"
    },
    {
      "reviewId": "Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tZd1NXdE9PRmxXT0daMlRrWTNORXB5UWtGSk1tYxAB",
      "authorName": "Roger Chang",
      "starRating": 5,
      "reviewDate": "3 months ago",
      "localGuideInfo": "Local Guide · 61 reviews",
      "text": "大禮堂於1954年建造完成，主建築外觀類似北京天壇，可容納約3400人與三峽博物館（就在對面）同為重慶標誌性建築，個人認為到重慶旅遊有多餘時間可到此同時參觀這兩大建築，了解重慶市的歷史及長江三峽的歷史文化.",
